title The window Rye raised -- macOS needs no Swift, and the Swift work is early rather than wasted
prompt Keaton asked whether macOS Tahoe needs a Swift wrapper for a GUI at all, whether it could be entirely Rye, and whether the Swift work is a waste; then gave the word for the probe and proposed yondering the Swift toward iOS publishing.
think The question was answerable by doing rather than arguing, so it was done: tools/rye/macos_window_probe.rye calls objc_getClass, sel_registerName, and objc_msgSend cast to exact signatures, fills its own 256x160 RGBA buffer, makes a CGImage of it, and sets it as the content view's layer contents.
think It raised a real window -- window_number=4648, the window server's own receipt -- and otool counts zero Swift libraries in the binary. The frameworks link straight through rye build with -lobjc -framework Cocoa -framework CoreGraphics.
think The one true fork is SwiftUI, which has no C ABI and no Objective-C interface. AppKit is entirely reachable; SwiftUI is not reachable at all. For a custom-drawn frame grid, that fork points away from Swift -- and the tree already drives Wayland (72 Rye modules) and Android NativeActivity the same way.
think The Swift work is early rather than wasted: the design is language-independent and ports, while iOS is where Swift stops being optional. The physical yonder of skate/ is a user-owned signed supervisor update -- the lane is spelled in a byte-pinned awk wall, the prompt, the receipt, and the roster -- so it is booked as a proposal rather than taken tonight.
obs Two Zig-dialect corrections on the way in, both cheap: std.Thread.sleep is absent in this toolchain (the tree's own nanosleep idiom answered), and callconv spells lowercase .c here. Everything else -- the ObjC casts, the CGRect by value, the framework links -- compiled first try.
obs The probe stays hand-run rather than rostered on purpose: it opens a window on somebody's screen, which is a rude thing for an unattended loop to do at three in the morning. The host tier would admit it; courtesy declines.
loom probe=macos_window_probe window_number=4648 frame=256x160 frame_bytes=163840 swift_libs_linked=0 binary_bytes=1895792
file tools/rye/macos_window_probe.rye the probe, bounded and asserted, with its build line in its header
